{"log": {"at": "2026-08-16T16:35:00-05:00", "msg": "Pointed the new rulebook at the nine hand-written presets. Ranked by worst width: landing 73, dashboard 67, masonry 62, document 61, docs 61, gallery 50, mail 49, shell 47, split 46. mail is B87 at 1280 and F49 at 390 — the sharpest argument on the site for scoring the WORST width rather than the mean. Three site-wide complaints fell out: --measure:52em is ~117 chars a line at 3440 (zero credit on five of nine), em padding does not scale (pad-share ~0 at 3440 on every preset), and repetition reads 0.95 on everything because web.js is made entirely of repeated components (real pages measure 0.23)."}}
{"log": {"at": "2026-08-16T16:36:00-05:00", "msg": "Three corrections to the rating tier found by running it on the presets: width-used had a CEILING that charged a full-bleed shell for spanning 99% — double-counting pad-shares complaint, now no upper penalty; width-used measured over text blocks only, so a gallery of sixteen image tiles reported spending 11% of 3440 while filling it — now over content leaves; and frame-gap/pad-share counted painted boxes with no text, so a wall of .wash swatches took frame-gap to 0.00 — now only boxes that hold text, the guard rules.js already has."}}
{"log": {"at": "2026-08-16T16:55:00-05:00", "msg": "Hunt run 1: 8 sweeps x 120 seeds x 3 widths. CHAOS HURTS MONOTONICALLY — mean worst at depth 2 is 60.5 at chaos 0, 59.0 at 0.25, 56.2 at 0.5, 51.0 at 1.0. That is the number the grammar was for: the model beats the flat pick it replaced by 16%. But the single best layout in the grid (worst 81) came from chaos 0.25, not chaos 0 — chaos widens the tail both ways, which is the argument for the dial rather than for loosening the model. Depth is nearly flat (1-4 span 2.4pts, best at 2). fit is a genuine null result (screen 1.001 vs page 0.998, n=296/184)."}}
{"log": {"at": "2026-08-16T16:57:00-05:00", "msg": "Threw out run 1s shape table: the three rater fixes landed AFTER the sweeps started, and two of them hit exactly the ranges run 1 named as discriminating. gallery and deck are the two text-poorest shapes and were the bottom two, while width-used was still measured over text blocks only. A search is only as good as the scorer it searches against, and the first thing a search finds is the scorers bugs. Re-running five sweeps against the corrected ranges before touching any weight in model.js."}}
{"assign": {"now": "hunt run 1 landed (chaos hurts 16%); re-running against the corrected ranges before retuning model.js. Docs and per-file notes in flight.", "step": 7, "links": [{"url": "/framework/dev/Claim/", "label": "dev/Claim — the tab claim ring"}, {"url": "/framework/ext/LayoutTool/taste/", "label": "LayoutTool taste — the eleven ideal ranges"}, {"url": "/framework/styles/layouts/space/", "label": "Space — the lab, now with a chaos dial and a live rating"}, {"url": "/framework/styles/layouts/space/hunt/", "label": "Hunt — the search, and where the model gets better"}]}}
