{"log": {"at": "2026-08-16T17:45:00-05:00", "msg": "Hunt run 2, against the corrected ranges. Seed 85 scored worst 63 under the old ranges and worst 87 under the new — same generator, same seed, a 24-point swing that was entirely the scorer. Chaos still hurts but by two thirds as much (-9.3% not -16%). The shape order RESHUFFLED: shell mid-table to first (lift 1.14), mail first to a four-way tie for third, gallery and deck recovered 8-10 points but are still the bottom two. Run 1s recommendation (raise mail) did not survive. model.js SHAPES now carries the run-2 numbers, each old weight scaled by lift cubed. Ceiling rose 81 to 87."}}
{"log": {"at": "2026-08-16T17:47:00-05:00", "msg": "The honest cost of the width-used fix: it went from run 1s third-best discriminator (gap 0.26) to exactly 0.00 — this generator now clears 70% width-use so reliably the range cannot separate a good roll from a bad one. Keeping its weight anyway, because the nine hand-written presets fail it hard at 3440: a range can be saturated for one population and the sharpest thing you own for another. Five ranges (slivers, depth, repetition, scale, gap-share) carry no information for the generator at all — a result rather than a gap, since the model keeps every roll clear of the zones they exist to catch."}}
